  {
   "id": "qss_step250_row23_col30_rain_budget_rescaling",
   "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 em_quarter_ss idealized supercell (GNU real32 build, dx = 2 km, dt = 12 s, 40 layers, WSM6 only), step 250 (t = 50 min), row j = 23, column i = 30 dumped by the instrumented ctessum-claude/WRF fork (module_esm_dump with the esm_dump_inner hooks inside mp_wsm6_run of the ctessum-claude/MMM-physics fork, commit 52cfbd7) and replayed through the real64 (kind_phys = real64) standalone kernels/wsm6_driver at the WRF step (dtcld = 12 s). POINTWISE in the sense of FORTRAN_BUGS.md N3: the mass-conservation rescaling and the update it feeds are dtcld-dependent by construction (every factor is 1 in the dtcld -> 0 limit), so the test compares them at the kernel's own sub-step instead of replaying at a small dt. Inputs are the state at which the kernel evaluates its rates (t_rates, q/qc/qi/qr/qs/qg_rates, i.e. after the sub-step's sedimentation, melting and freezing), the start-of-sub-step xl and cpm (note N4) and the 22 dumped `<rate>_raw` rates (each after its own per-process limiter, before this block); the expected values are the dumped `<rate>_final` rates, the dumped `*_upd` state and the tendencies (q_upd - q_rates)/dtcld and (t_upd - t_rates)/dtcld from the same replay. The conservation factors are read back from the dump as the ratio of a rate that carries exactly ONE factor (prevp -> f_qr, pidep -> f_qi, psdep -> f_qs, pgdep -> f_qg). This block contains no physical constant beyond T0, xls, qmin, qcrmin and the 1e-4 kg/kg partition threshold, and every input is dumped, so the real64 replay is reproduced to machine precision. Regime: the glaciated flank of the storm -- snow 2.7e-3 and graupel 6.3e-3 kg/kg dominate, cloud water reaches 4.2e-4 and rain only 1.3e-5 kg/kg, with 7 layers above 0 C at the bottom. This is the column in which the RAIN budget binds hardest anywhere in the dumped set: accretion of the little rain that is left by snow and graupel (psacr + pgacr) together with its freezing on ice would remove more than the available qr in one sub-step, so f_qr = 0.7146 at layer 15 and 0.5877 at layer 16, and prevp, pracw, piacr, psacr and pgacr are all scaled by it there. The cloud-water and graupel budgets are not overdrawn (f_qc = f_qg = 1) and the ice budget binds only at the 1e-16 level. Residual (esm vs the real64 replay, measured with zero tolerances): all 22 `<rate>_final` columns, the cold/delta2/delta3 switches and all seven updated fields are reproduced EXACTLY (0.0); the only nonzero residuals are the two tendencies, dqv_dt 5.1e-20 kg/kg/s (2.2e-14 of the column maximum) and dT_dt 2.3e-15 K/s (3.5e-13 of the column maximum), which is summation-order rounding of the latent-heat sum. Tolerances are set at 1e-9 of each rate column's maximum, 1e-12 of each updated field's maximum and rel 1e-12 on the factor spot checks -- four to five orders above the measured residual; the switches keep zero tolerance.",
